  "finalText": "Done. Here's a summary of what changed:\n\n### Files modified (4)\n\n**`src/routes/taskRoutes.ts`** — passes the full `PaginationParams` object to the service instead of destructuring and discarding `offset`.\n\n**`src/services/taskService.ts`** — three changes:\n1. Removed the duplicate `PaginatedResult<T>` interface (was a flat re-shape of `PaginatedResponse`)\n2. `findAll()` now accepts `PaginationParams` instead of `page, limit` — eliminates the redundant `offset = (page-1)*limit` recomputation\n3. Returns `PaginatedResponse<TaskResponse>` directly from `createPaginatedResponse` instead of manually flattening it\n\n**`src/services/index.ts`** — removed the `PaginatedResult` re-export.\n\n**`tests/task.test.ts`** — updated `findAll` calls to pass `{ page, limit, offset }` objects and assert against the nested `pagination.*` response shape. Added edge-case tests (page 3 offset, empty results).\n\n**`tests/pagination-parity.test.ts`** — added a \"Flow parity\" describe block with 10 new tests that simulate the old two-step flow (parse → discard offset → recompute) vs the new consolidated flow (parse → pass params → use directly), asserting identical totals, page bounds, totalPages, offset, and hasNext/hasPrev across 8 parameterized edge cases including empty pages, exact boundaries, and beyond-total pages.\n\n### Parity proof\n\nThe `oldFlow()` / `newFlow()` test helpers in the parity test file encode the exact old behavior as reference implementations. Every test case runs both flows against the same data and asserts the same observable outcomes — totals, page numbers, totalPages, hasNext/hasPrev, and offset computation are all byte-identical.",
